{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791594542,"nonce":"9SpdPHqnfIxL/X7Ism3Z6YTIUtw=","message":"Defaults landed (2026-10-10): the theme no longer carries its own :root rule. blinc_ts/theme/user-agent sets the window's ground, ink and type from the theme and gives built-in elements their looks, and baseUiTheme relies on it. The adapter test adds it first, as an app would.\n\nWhy it was needed: every built-in tag is a flex row with no look of its own, so a div laid children side by side and an h1 was body text. Reading it also showed that Host.createElement never described a plain element to the cascade, so no type selector could match; that is fixed.\n\nStill open for this issue, and ranked in the issue titled \"Ports from ashui, in priority order\": the top layer (Popover, Tooltip, Select, Menu, Dialog), inline text flow for the wiki's prose, scrollbars, list markers and the other built-in element behaviours, and motion. The component set for the wiki is not chosen yet.","files":null}]}